;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally with `jolt site:serve`. There is
;; deliberately NO GitHub Pages site (`.github/workflows/site.yml` only builds
;; it, run by hand): this repo is private
;; and staying that way for now. Publishing is two separate decisions, taken
;; explicitly, and neither is implied by this file existing. Until the
;; project is open-sourced, the only way to see this site is to build it on
;; your own machine.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one. Every
 ;; URL the engine emits carries this prefix. Leave it out and the pages still
 ;; render, each one loading the ORGANIZATION site's stylesheet while every
 ;; asset 404s, which is a quiet way to ship a broken site.
 :base-path   "/jonquil"

 :title       "Jonquil"
 :description "A DrRacket-style Clojure IDE written in Jolt: a Definitions editor, an Interactions console, Run and a Stop that really stops."

 ;; docs/images holds the screenshots and the GIF the guide pages reference;
 ;; copying it into the build is what keeps ../images/foo.png resolving from
 ;; a rendered guide page.
 :asset-dirs  ["images"]}
